      {
        "title": "Ezekiel's Denunciations of Judah",
        "introduction": "Over the next five years, from 591 to 586 B.C., Ezekiel brings a number of denunciations against Judah for its idolatry, its false prophets, its corrupt leaders, its rebellious spirit, its religious infidelity, and its sins. An introduction to these denunciations comes in the form of a most unusual occurrence. Ezekiel says that God took him to Jerusalem to show him the idolatry in the temple and the punishment of idolaters and corrupt leaders, and then returned him to his house in Tel Aviv. It all happens somehow while Ezekiel is sitting in his house in the presence of a group of elders."
